            <ArticleTitle>Causality, linearity, and circularity of relations between stressful life events and pain experience.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>85-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aim of this paper is to point out a methodological problem found in the 1994 Naidoo and Pillay study on pain experience. The problem is that an equivocal interpretation of cause-and-effect relationships among variables can lead to testing of mistaken hypotheses in later researches.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
